message.reasoning:
The user wants us to generate two sound files: test.wav (440Hz sine, 5s) and test2.wav (880Hz square, 10s). Then play them with specified volumes. We have two functions: generate_sound_wave and play_sound_wave. We'll call generate_sound_wave twice with appropriate parameters. Then call play_sound_wave twice.

We need to output calls to the functions. According to guidelines, we should not provide additional text beyond function calls. So we will produce two function calls for generate_sound_wave, then two for play_sound_wave. Each call must be separate JSON objects. The order matters: first generate test.wav, then generate test2.wav, then play test.wav, then play test2.wav.

We need to specify wave_type for second as "square". For first, default is sine so we can omit or specify "sine".

Also we need to specify filenames: wave_file: "test.wav" etc.

Volume defaults to 1 if omitted; but we need to set volume for play calls: 0.8 and 0.6.

Thus we produce:

{
  "name": "generate_sound_wave",
  "arguments": {
    "frequency": 440,
    "duration": 5,
    "wave_type": "sine"
  }
}

Then second generate:

{
  "name": "generate_sound_wave",
  "arguments": {
    "frequency": 880,
    "duration": 10,
    "wave_type": "square"
  }
}

Then play test.wav:

{
  "name": "play_sound_wave",
  "arguments": {
    "wave_file": "test.wav",
    "volume": 0.8
  }
}

Then play test2.wav:

{
  "name": "play_sound_wave",
  "arguments": {
    "wave_file": "test2.wav",
    "volume": 0.6
  }
}

We need to output each JSON object on its own line. No extra text.
